.TH amtterm 1 "(c) 2007 Gerd Hoffmann"
.SH NAME
amtterm - Intel AMT serial-over-lan (sol) client.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amtterm [ options ] host
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B amtterm
provides access to the serial-over-lan port of Intel AMT managed
machines.

.B host
Hostname or IP address of the machine amtterm should connect to.
.P
For more inforamtions on Intel AMT check amt-howto(7).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h
Display help text.
.TP
.B -v
Be verbose.
.TP
.B -q
Be quiet (default).
.TP
.B -u <user>
Specify username, defaults to "admin".
.TP
.B -p <pass>
Specify password.

.B amtterm
will prompt on the terminal if password not provded.
.TP
.B -d
Debug output.
.TP
.B -L
Enable SSL and use legacy SSL authentication.
.TP
.B -A
enable SSL and use System Trust Store.
.TP
.B -N
Enable SSL and allow insecure server connections.
.TP
.B -C
Enable SSL and use PEM cacert file.
.TP
.B -c clientcert -k clientkey:pass
Enable mutual TLS and specify client certificate and client key (with
optional passphrase).

.B amtterm
will prompt on the terminal if the passphrase is not specified.
.SH SEE ALSO
amttool(1), amt-howto(7)
